{#-
  The colour-scheme control. Included by a layout only when
  `site.theme_switch` is on, which is off by default.

  Two pieces and both are deliberate.

  The **head script** runs before first paint, which is why it is inline and
  why it is first: reading the stored choice after the stylesheet has painted
  would show the wrong scheme and then correct it, and a flash of the scheme
  a reader turned off is worse than not offering the control. It is the only
  script this tool emits.

  The **button ships hidden and the script unhides it.** A control that did
  nothing without JavaScript would be worse than an absent one, and hiding it
  from CSS alone would leave it in the accessibility tree; `hidden` removes it
  from both. So a reader without JavaScript sees no control and gets the
  scheme their operating system asks for, which is what they got before this
  existed.

  `data-theme` is read by `assets/tokens.css`, which every theme generates
  from its own tokens, so this works for any palette without knowing one.
-#}
<script>
(function () {
  try {
    var stored = localStorage.getItem("iyo-theme");
    if (stored === "light" || stored === "dark") {
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", stored);
    }
  } catch (e) {
    /* Private mode, or storage disabled: the OS preference still applies. */
  }
})();
</script>
